===== FINDING: interior control char in Write file_path (SEC-02) =====
file_path=".harness/events.jsonl\nJUNK" (interior newline) -> ALLOW (hook returns null, no judgment)
file_path="src/app.ts\nJUNK"           -> ALLOW
file_path=".harness/events.jsonl\n" (TRAILING) -> DENY (trimmed)  ; leading \n -> DENY ; \r/\t trailing -> DENY
On disk the interior-newline path is a DISTINCT filename (realpath != real core), so NO write-through
of the protected file occurs at the OS layer. Bounded impact; escalation depends on whether the
downstream Write tool normalizes interior newlines (untested here).

